---
// The "Treadmill" label (T155, FR-058): shown wherever a run with `treadmill: true` appears (the
// latest-run card, run pages, and later the run list and race history). A treadmill run's distance
// is the watch's estimate, so it counts toward totals and the training build but not PBs or
// race-time goals unless the owner includes it, and it never has a map. The label is text, not
// colour alone, so it reads the same to everyone and to assistive tech. No client JS.
---

<span class="treadmill-badge" data-treadmill>
  <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14">
    <path d="M2 12h12M3 12l2-7h7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
  </svg>
  Treadmill
</span>

<style>
  .treadmill-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0 var(--space-2);
    border: 1px solid currentColor;
    border-radius: var(--radius-mark);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    line-height: 1.6;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
